\b Process Flow\b0 \par
1. Users, masters, and permissions are prepared.\par
2. Cross-desk workflows are monitored during pilot use.\par
3. Configuration gaps and adoption blockers are identified.\par
4. Platform behavior is tuned based on live feedback.\par
\par
\b How To Operate In Josh\b0 \par
1. Start by reviewing cross-desk adoption, user access issues, master-data gaps, and workflow blockers across the pilot.\par
2. Use Admin Masters, User Master, Rights Matrix, and Onboarding as the control points for setup correction and access readiness.\par
3. Open the affected operational desk directly in Josh when a user reports a broken handoff, missing visibility, or process confusion.\par
4. Use Product Master, templates, and policy screens to correct root-cause setup instead of applying temporary offline workarounds.\par
5. Keep Josh as the single operating control layer for pilot monitoring, escalation, and tuning decisions.\par
\par
\b How You Should Operate Daily\b0 \par
1. Monitor pilot access and user setup.\par
2. Review cross-desk blockers and escalation points.\par
3. Maintain masters, templates, and rights.\par
4. Guide process correction and platform tuning.\par
\par
\b What To Watch Carefully\b0 \par
- Watch for repeated access issues, master gaps, and cross-desk blockers that point to setup or policy problems.\par
- Check whether users are solving workflow gaps inside Josh or falling back to temporary offline practices.\par
- Watch for weak ownership in rights, templates, and policy settings that affects pilot adoption.\par
- Capture system-wide improvements that will make the pilot easier to scale after stabilization.\par
\par
